# Numeric coercion and type checks as modules write them: coercion types
# in signatures, .Int/.Rat/.Num/.Numeric on strings, prefix +, allomorphs,
# val(), .narrow, .nude, FatRat, and `~~ Int` / `~~ Real` checks.

=== num-coerce-int-param-str
from: Backtrace::Files 0.0.4 lib/Backtrace/Files.rakumod:108
license: Artistic-2.0
feature: param coercion Int()
--- code
my @lines;
my sub add(str $string, Int() $linenr) {
    @lines.push: "$linenr: $string ({$linenr.^name})";
}
add('first', '12');
add('second', 3.9);
add('third', 7);
.say for @lines;
--- expect
12: first (Int)
3: second (Int)
7: third (Int)

=== num-coerce-int-my-decl
